% The work naive evaluation does on a chain, as counted by -X stats.  Every
% pass joins every path with every edge again, so each path is rederived in
% every pass after the one that first derived it; stats-semi-naive.dl is the
% same program under the default fixed point.  Both use the textual planner,
% so that the counts measure the fixed point alone.

edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
edge(c, d).
edge(d, e).
edge(e, f).
edge(f, g).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- path(X, Y), edge(Y, Z).

path(a, X)?
